</table> </div> <p style="margin-top:18pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><span style="font-style:italic">Revenue</span>,<span style="font-style:italic"> net</span> </p> <p style="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:9%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Revenue, net for the three months ended June&#160;30, 2023 was $16.3&#160;million, a $3.8&#160;million or a 30% increase compared to revenue, net of $12.5&#160;million for the three months ended June&#160;30, 2022. This change is explained by a $0.4&#160;million increase in revenues resulting from the continued demand for our services from our existing clients and a $3.4&#160;million increase in revenues generated from new clients. </p> <p style="margin-top:18pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><span style="font-style:italic">Cost of Revenue </span></p> <p style="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:9%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Cost of revenue for the three months ended June&#160;30, 2023 was $11.9&#160;million, and $3.0&#160;million or a 34% increase compared to cost of revenue of $8.9&#160;million for the three months ended June&#160;30, 2022. $1.9&#160;million of the increase was driven by an increase in compensation and benefit costs as a result of an increase in our client-serving headcount to support revenue growth, and the remainder was driven by an increase in other expenses associated with fulfilling our contracts with customers. </p>
 <p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt ; font-size:8pt">&#160;</p> <p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman;text-align:center">219 </p>

</div></div>



<p style="margin-top:1em; margin-bottom:0em; page-break-before:always"> </p>
<hr style="color:#999999;height:3px;width:100%"/>
<h5><a href="#toc">Table of Contents</a></h5>


<div style="text-align:center"><div style="width:8.5in;text-align:left;margin-left: auto;margin-right: auto">
 <p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><span style="font-style:italic">Gross Profit </span></p> <p style="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:9%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Gross profit for three months ended June&#160;30, 2023 was $4.4&#160;million, a $0.7 million or a 21% increase compared to gross profit of $3.7 million for the three months ended June&#160;30, 2022. The higher gross profit in the three months ended June&#160;30, 2023 was primarily driven by the $3.8&#160;million increase in revenue attributable to the increased demand for services from new and existing clients, which was offset by a $2.8&#160;million increase in cost of revenue mainly due to the increased compensation costs and other expenses associated with fulfilling our contracts with customers. </p> <div> <p style="margin-top:18pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><span style="font-style:italic">Gross Profit Margin </span></p> <p style="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:9%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Gross profit margin for the three months ended June&#160;30, 2023 was 27%, a 2% decrease compared to gross profit margin of 29% for the three months ended June&#160;30, 2022. The decrease is primarily due to increased compensation costs and other expenses associated with fulfilling our contracts with customers. </p> </div> <p style="margin-top:18pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><span style="font-style:italic">Selling, general and administrative </span></p> <p style="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:9%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Selling and administrative expenses for the three months ended June&#160;30, 2023 were $3.7&#160;million, a $1.6&#160;million and 74% increase, compared to selling and administrative expenses of $2.1&#160;million for the three months ended June&#160;30, 2022. Increased stock-based compensation accounted for approximately $1.4&#160;million of the increase. The remainder of the increase was attributable to costs associated with expanding our operations that required increased levels of hiring resulting in increased personnel-related costs. </p> <p style="margin-top:18pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><span style="font-style:italic">Other income (expense), net </span></p> <p style="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:9%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Other expense, net for the three months ended June&#160;30, 2023 was $0.1&#160;million, a $0.3&#160;million and 130% decrease, compared to other income, net of $0.2&#160;million for the three months ended June&#160;30, 2022. The increase was mainly due to an exchange gain recorded for the three months ended June&#160;30, 2022 as a result of favorable exchange rate movement. </p> <p style="margin-top:18pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><span style="font-style:italic">Provision for income taxes</span></p> <p style="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:9%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Provision for income taxes for three months ended June&#160;30, 2023 was $0.2&#160;million, a $0.2&#160;million and 49% decrease compared to provision of income taxes of $0.4&#160;million for three months ended June&#160;30, 2022. The decrease was primarily due to the significant decrease in <span style="white-space:nowrap">pre-tax</span> income during the period.</p> <p style="margin-top:18pt; margin-bottom:0pt; margin-left:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><span style="font-weight:bold"><span style="white-space:nowrap">Non-GAAP</span> Financial Measures</span> </p> <p style="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:9%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">We use <span style="white-space:nowrap">non-GAAP</span> financial information and believe it is useful to investors as it provides additional information to facilitate comparisons of historical operating results, identify trends in our underlying operating results and provide additional insight and transparency on how we evaluate the business. We use <span style="white-space:nowrap">non-GAAP</span> financial measures to budget, make operating and strategic decisions, and evaluate our performance. We have detailed the <span style="white-space:nowrap">non-GAAP</span> adjustments that we make in our <span style="white-space:nowrap">non-GAAP</span> definitions below. The adjustments generally fall within the categories of <span style="white-space:nowrap">non-cash</span> items. We believe the <span style="white-space:nowrap">non-GAAP</span> measures presented herein should always be considered along with, and not as a substitute for or superior to, the related GAAP financial measures. We have provided the reconciliations between the GAAP and <span style="white-space:nowrap">non-GAAP</span> financial measures below, and we also discuss our underlying GAAP results throughout the Management&#8217;s Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations section. </p> <p style="margin-top:18pt; margin-bottom:0pt; margin-left:9%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman;font-weight:bold"><span style="font-style:italic">Adjusted EBITDA </span></p> <p style="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:9%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">We define Adjusted EBITDA as net income from operations before interest, income taxes, depreciation and amortization adjusted to exclude stock-based compensation and business combination related costs. Adjusted </p>
 <p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt ; font-size:8pt">&#160;</p> <p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman;text-align:center">220 </p>

</div></div>



<p style="margin-top:1em; margin-bottom:0em; page-break-before:always"> </p>
<hr style="color:#999999;height:3px;width:100%"/>
<h5><a href="#toc">Table of Contents</a></h5>


<div style="text-align:center"><div style="width:8.5in;text-align:left;margin-left: auto;margin-right: auto">
 <p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">
EBITDA is one of the key performance indicators we use in evaluating our operating performance and in making financial, operating, and planning decisions. We believe adjusted EBITDA is useful to the investors of this proxy statement in the evaluation of Aeries&#8217; operating performance as such information was used by securities analysts and other interested parties as a measure of financial information and debt service capabilities, and it was used by our management for internal reporting and planning procedures, including aspects of our consolidated operating budget and capital expenditures. </p> <div> <p style="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:9%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">The following table provides a reconciliation from net income (GAAP measure) to EBITDA and adjusted EBITDA (Non-GAAP measures) for the years ended March 31, 2023, and March 31, 2022 (in thousands): </p> </div> <p style="font-size:12pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt">&#160;</p> <div>
